{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the fixed cost f_k incurred only if station k is actually used (i.e., some positive quantity is transshipped through it), and is it added once per used station regardless of how much flows through it?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy confirmation regarding the trigger condition and the application frequency of the fixed cost, which constitutes one semantically independent clarification."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "is it acceptable to leave some production unused (i.e., ship less than a_i from a production point), or must each production point ship exactly its full output a_i?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding whether production output must be fully utilized or can be partially unused."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the demand points: must each demand point j receive exactly its full demand b_j, or is it acceptable to leave some demand unmet (receive less than b_j)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question about whether demand must be fully met or if unmet demand is allowed."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the objective: is the goal to minimize the total cost, where total cost equals the sum of (unit cost × quantity) for all legs (production→station and station→demand) plus the fixed cost f_k for each station that is used?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the specific objective function definition."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the transshipment capacity constraint \"total quantity transshipped through each intermediate marshaling station k must not exceed its maximum capacity q_k\": does the transshipped quantity at station k equal the total quantity arriving at k from all production points (which should equal the total quantity leaving k to all demand points), and is this total what is capped at q_k?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for confirmation of a single specific definition regarding the capacity constraint variable. Although it contains two clauses connected by 'and', they are verifying the same semantic concept (the definition of the quantity being capped), so they constitute one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the fixed cost and capacity interaction: if station k is used (some positive quantity flows through it), is the capacity q_k still enforced as a hard upper bound on the transshipped quantity, or does paying the fixed cost f_k remove the capacity limit?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the capacity limit remains a hard bound or is removed when the fixed cost is paid."
}

